        "DEFINITION": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DEFINITION",
          "canonical_heading": "DEFINITION",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "A systemic autoimmune disease characterized by the formation of antibodies against a wide array of self-antigens. Pathogenic antibodies, circulating immune complexes, and auto reactive T-cells are the primary mediators of tissue injury.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "PATHOPHYSIOLOGY": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "PATHOPHYSIOLOGY",
          "canonical_heading": "PATHOPHYSIOLOGY",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Antigen–antibody complexes are formed and deposited in a variety of sites, including blood vessels, glomeruli, synovial membranes, choroid plexus, and skin (type III hypersensitivity).",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Antibodies directed against a broad range of membrane, cytoplasmic, and nuclear antigens are produced, resulting in direct cytotoxic damage (type II hypersensitivity).",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Production of autoreactive T-cells causes cell-mediated damage (type IV hypersensitivity).",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Tissue injury is caused by immune-complex mediated activation of complement, infiltration of inflammatory cells, and direct cytotoxicity of autoantibodies against membrane-bound antigens.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Clinical manifestations depend on localization of the immune complexes and specificity of the autoantibodies.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Genetic, environmental, pharmacologic, and infectious factors may be triggers.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "SYSTEMS AFFECTED": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SYSTEMS AFFECTED",
          "canonical_heading": "SYSTEMS AFFECTED",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Musculoskeletal—deposition of immune complexes in synovial membranes.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Skin/exocrine—deposition of immune complexes in the skin.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Renal/urologic—immune-complex glomerulonephritis.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Hemic/lymphatic/immune—autoantibodies against red blood cells (RBCs), leukocytes, platelets, and bone marrow precursors.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Other organ systems—associated with deposition of immune complexes or antibodies.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "GENETICS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "GENETICS",
          "canonical_heading": "GENETICS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "In dogs, SLE has been positively associated with the presence of dog leukocyte antigen (DLA) A7 and negatively associated with the presence of DLA A1 and B5. Decreased serum IgA has been reported as a predisposing factor for SLE in dogs.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "An immune-mediated disease in the Nova Scotia duck tolling retriever characterized by immune-mediated arthropathy and steroidresponsive meningitis–arteritis has been reported and is termed SLE-related disease in this breed.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "INCIDENCE/PREVALENCE": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "INCIDENCE/PREVALENCE",
          "canonical_heading": "INCIDENCE/PREVALENCE",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Uncommon in dog, rare in cat.",
              "pdf_page": 927,
              "printed_page": 845,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
